Package: maluos-gateway
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, python3 (>= 3.12), python3-aiohttp, python3-psycopg, python3-yaml,
 systemd (>= 250), curl, zstd, maluos-firstboot (>= 0.1.5), maluos-vault (>= 0.1.0)
Recommends: postgresql-18-maludb-core, maludb-mc2dbd
Description: MaluOS inference gateway: one door to local and cloud models
 A daemon on a Unix socket (and optionally a token-protected TCP port) that
 serves the OpenAI and Ollama APIs, identifies callers by their Linux uid
 (peer credentials) and MaluDB principal, resolves tiers and aliases to
 backend models under per-principal policy, schedules the single local GPU
 (priority classes, fairness between principals, model affinity, expected
 wait) and records every call in the ledger. Drains the MaluDB engine's
 model request queue as batch work and exposes maluos.model_status as an
 MCP tool on the listener.
 .
 Ships `maluctl gateway`, a pinned installer for Ollama as a localhost-only
 service, a mock backend for tests, and the first-boot component that
 provisions the gateway. Phase 6 slice 2 of MaluOS.
